Performance: Gates

Purpose:
  Defines performance gates including load testing and DDoS resilience.

PerformanceGates:
  LoadGate:
    Format: LOAD-GATE-<ID>
    Condition: System handles expected load
    Evidence: load test report
    Metrics:
      - RPS
      - P50
      - P95
      - P99
      - Error rate
      - CPU
      - Memory
      - DB latency
      - Cache hit rate
      - Queue latency
    Threshold: Context-dependent
    Owner: QA/DevOps

  DDoSResilienceGate:
    Format: DDOS-GATE-<ID>
    Condition: System withstands DDoS simulation
    Evidence: resilience test report
    Checks:
      - Rate limiting
      - WAF
      - CDN
      - Load balancer
      - Autoscaling
    Owner: DevOps/Security
    Note: Agent does NOT execute real DDoS; creates controlled test plan.

PerformanceRules:
  [PF1]  Load testing is context-dependent (not all projects need it).
  [PF2]  DDoS gate uses controlled simulation, not real attacks.
  [PF3]  Performance thresholds are based on project scale.
  [PF4]  Performance gate failure blocks release for L3+.

State: +
  